{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyCfx2AmTJbDNm6S9SYG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Audit Conclusion: T6S2 Payroll Engine Golden-Snapshot Gate\n\n## Assessment\n\n**1. Gate design is acceptable as-is; no changes required; second-major proof is NOT required.**\n\n## Rationale\n\n- **ADR 007 (2026-03-02) documents an explicit, deliberate runtime pin.** The decision predates any gate incident and is justified on grounds of bitwise reproducibility for historical payroll integrity—a legitimate operational constraint in financial systems. This satisfies the \"documented before the red\" requirement (operational-rigor §3).\n\n- **The pin is enforced across all execution tiers** (CI, production, `package.json`), making it an active, enforceable constraint, not a suggestion.\n\n- **The governing doctrine is clear:** *\"A runtime pinned as a recorded decision — documented before the red, not relabelled after it — owes no proof of a claim it never made.\"* The payroll engine **never claimed portability across Node majors.** It claimed the opposite: Node 20 only, for reproducibility.\n\n- **A second-major proof would prove the wrong thing.** Passing on Node 22 would demonstrate *that runtime is stable*, not that *this product is portable*. The gate is green precisely because it runs on its pinned environment. A second-major pass would silence the teammate's concern while handing the same fragility to the next unplanned runtime drift (violating the stopgap rule).\n\n- **The numeric contract is implicit in the pin:** \"bitwise reproducibility under Node 20.\" The full-precision `npv` serialization is fit-for-purpose *under that constraint*.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nDocument the ADR reference **in the gate's inline comment or test preamble** if not already present, so future maintainers see the pin rationale at audit time. Do **not** add a second-major test or relax the engine constraint without a new ADR reversing the 2026-03-02 decision."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":451,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
